.TH "C3L" "1" "2026-11-03"
.P
.SH NAME
.P
\fBc3l\fR - reproducible dependencies for C3 projects, for any \fBc3c fetch\fR registry.\&
.P
.SH SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBc3l\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
\fBc3l\fR \fB--version\fR | \fB--help\fR | \fBhelp\fR [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.P
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
\fBc3c fetch\fR installs libraries but records no version, verifies no checksum and
cannot update or remove.\& \fBc3l\fR adds a lockfile, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR, checksum
verification with rollback, and update, outdated, remove and sync.\& Libraries are
kept as \fI.\&c3l\fR zip files in the first entry of \fIdependency-search-paths\fR.\& Run
\fBc3l\fR in the project root.\&
.P
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.P
\fBc3l\fR is linked against \fBlibcurl\fR.\& At run time it calls \fBc3c\fR (to read the project
with \fBc3c project view\fR, for \fBinit\fR and for the compile check of \fBcheck\fR) and \fBgit\fR
(git libraries, \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR, \fBpublish\fR).\& It talks to registries itself, with the
protocol \fBc3c fetch\fR uses, so any \fBc3c\fR that can build the project will do.\&
.P
.SH OPTIONS
.P
The options from \fB--registry\fR to \fB--registry-type\fR may appear before or after the
command.\& The publishing options, from \fB--version\fR to \fB--offline\fR, follow \fBcheck\fR,
\fBpack\fR or \fBpublish\fR.\&
.P
\fB--registry\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB--registry=\fR\fIURL\fR
.RS 4
Use this registry base URL for the command (as \fBc3c --fetch-url\fR takes it, path
included).\& Overrides \fBC3L_REGISTRY\fR.\& It picks the registry for \fBadd\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBinfo\fR
and \fBpublish\fR; libraries already in \fIc3l.\&lock\fR are always fetched from the registry
recorded for them.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--dry-run\fR
.RS 4
Only print what \fBupdate\fR or \fBprune\fR would change, or stop \fBpublish\fR before the
upload.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--frozen\fR
.RS 4
For \fBsync\fR, meant for CI.\& Fail if \fIproject.\&json\fR and \fIc3l.\&lock\fR list different
libraries, restore only what the lockfile says, and never write the lockfile.\&
Has no effect on other commands.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--strict\fR
.RS 4
With \fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR: fail instead of warn when the registry says a library
was published for another C3 release than your \fBc3c\fR (compared by
major.\&minor), or does not list your platform, and when libraries require each
other in a cycle or a library requires itself.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--fail-fast\fR
.RS 4
With \fBsync\fR and \fBupdate\fR: stop at the first library that fails.\& The default is to
go on with the others and report the failures at the end (exit status 1).\&
.P
.RE
\fB--force\fR
.RS 4
With \fBremove\fR: remove the library even if another library requires it.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--allow-host\fR \fIHOST\fR
.RS 4
Trust \fIHOST\fR for git or registry dependencies named by a library'\&s \fIc3l.\&lock\fR or
\fImanifest.\&json\fR.\& Local paths and \fBfile://\fR URLs are the host \fIfile\fR.\& Can be
repeated.\& See \fBDEPENDENCIES\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--registry-type\fR \fIstatic|c3pkg\fR
.RS 4
Override the detected registry type.\& See \fBPUBLISHING\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--version\fR \fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR, \fB--version=\fR\fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR
.RS 4
After \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR or \fBpublish\fR: the version to publish.\& Before any command,
\fB--version\fR prints the version of \fBc3l\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--token-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
File with the registry API token (first line).\& See \fBPUBLISHING\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--description\fR \fITEXT\fR, \fB--license\fR \fIID\fR, \fB--tags\fR \fIa,b\fR, \fB--docs-url\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB--git-url\fR \fIURL\fR
.RS 4
Package metadata for \fBpublish\fR.\& The description is required the first time a
package is published.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--c3-version\fR \fIX.\&Y.\&Z\fR
.RS 4
C3 version sent to the registry.\& Default: the version of \fBc3c\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--output\fR \fIFILE\fR
.RS 4
For \fBpack\fR: where to write the package.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--allow-dirty\fR
.RS 4
Let \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and \fBpublish\fR run on a working tree with uncommitted changes.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--no-build\fR
.RS 4
Skip the compile check in \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and \fBpublish\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fB--offline\fR
.RS 4
Do not query the registry in \fBcheck\fR (the registry is always skipped by \fBpack\fR).\&
.P
.RE
\fB--tree\fR
.RS 4
After \fBlist\fR: print the dependency graph instead of the table.\&
.P
.RE
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Print the usage text, of \fBc3l\fR or of the command it follows.\&
.P
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.P
Some commands have short names: \fBadd\fR is also \fBfetch\fR, \fBf\fR, \fBget\fR and \fBg\fR; \fBremove\fR is
\fBrm\fR, \fBr\fR and \fBdelete\fR; \fBupdate\fR is \fBu\fR; \fBsync\fR is \fBpull\fR and \fBp\fR; \fBlist\fR is \fBls\fR and \fBl\fR;
\fBsearch\fR is \fBs\fR.\&
.P
\fBinit\fR [\fIname\fR]
.RS 4
Create \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& With \fIname\fR and outside a project, run \fBc3c init\fR first.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fInamespace/name\fR[@\fIversion\fR]
.RS 4
Install a library from the registry, compare the SHA-256 of the download with
the registry'\&s checksum, write the lock line.\& The version can also be given as a
separate argument.\& A mismatch or any failure restores the previous library file
and \fIproject.\&json\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR vendor:\fIname\fR, \fBadd\fR vendor
.RS 4
Install a library from c3c'\&s vendor collection (the files of the \fIc3lang/vendor\fR
release \fIlatest\fR, what \fBc3c vendor-fetch\fR downloads).\& The collection has no
versions, so the lock pins the SHA-256 that GitHub lists for the file (kind
\fIvendor\fR, version \fIlatest\fR).\& \fBsync\fR fails if the file changed upstream; \fBoutdated\fR
shows such a change and \fBupdate\fR re-pins it.\& If no digest is listed, c3l warns and
records the download.\& Plain \fBadd vendor\fR lists the collection.\& A library may
require one with \fI"source": "vendor:name"\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fI.\&/dir\fR
.RS 4
Link a local library directory (\fI.\&/dir\fR, \fI.\&.\&/dir\fR or an absolute path with a
\fImanifest.\&json\fR) into \fIlib/\fR with a relative symlink, so edits show up in the next
build and the project and the directory can move together.\& \fBverify\fR checks where
the link points.\&
Recorded in the lockfile as kind \fIpath\fR; \fBsync\fR re-creates the link, \fBupdate\fR skips
it, and its own dependencies are followed.\& A library that depends on a local
directory cannot be published.\&
.P
.RE
\fBadd\fR \fIgit-url\fR[@\fIref\fR]
.RS 4
Install from a git repository.\& \fIref\fR is a tag, a branch, \fBHEAD\fR, or a full
40-character commit hash; it can also be given as a separate argument.\& Without
a \fIref\fR the highest release tag is used (prerelease tags such as \fIv1.\&0.\&0-rc.\&1\fR only
when asked for), or HEAD if there are none.\& The ref is resolved to a commit,
which is what the lockfile pins.\& \fBoutdated\fR and \fBupdate\fR move a tag to the
highest release tag and follow the tip of \fBHEAD\fR and of branches; commits stay
put; a tag only moves within its major version.\& In scp-style URLs (\fIgit@host:path\fR) the \fB@\fR only starts a ref after the
last \fB/\fR.\& URLs with credentials (\fIhttps://user:token@host/.\&.\&.\&\fR) are refused: the
URL is written to the lockfile; see \fBPRIVATE REPOSITORIES\fR.\& The library is built with \fBgit archive\fR, so no \fI.\&git\fR is included, and without
line-ending conversion.\& A git library is identified by its commit and its files:
the lockfile pins the commit and records a hash of the files in the archive, and
\fBverify\fR and \fBsync\fR check both (\fBgit archive\fR stores the commit id in the zip
comment).\& The hash covers names and contents only, so it does not depend on the
git version that built the archive.\& This needs \fBgit\fR.\& The repository needs a \fImanifest.\&json\fR at its root.\&
.P
.RE
\fBremove\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Delete the library file, its \fIdependencies\fR entry and its lock line.\& Refuses if
another library requires it (\fB--force\fR overrides) and lists libraries that are no
longer needed.\&
.P
.RE
\fBprune\fR
.RS 4
Remove dependency libraries that no directly added library needs any more.\&
With \fB--dry-run\fR only list them.\&
.P
.RE
\fBwhy\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Show which libraries require \fIname\fR, and why they are installed.\&
.P
.RE
\fBlist\fR [\fB--tree\fR]
.RS 4
Show every locked library with its state: \fIok\fR, \fImodified\fR, \fImissing\fR,
\fIunpacked\fR, and \fIuntracked\fR for libraries in \fIproject.\&json\fR not in the lockfile.\&
\fIdep\fR marks a library pulled in by another one.\& With \fB--tree\fR print the
dependency graph.\&
.P
.RE
\fBverify\fR
.RS 4
Check installed files against the lockfile.\& Exit status 1 on any difference.\&
.P
.RE
\fBoutdated\fR
.RS 4
Show locked libraries for which the registry (or git) has a higher version: the
newest of the same major version, which \fBupdate\fR moves to, and a newer major
version if there is one.\& A library whose source cannot be reached is named, and
the exit status is 1.\&
.P
.RE
\fBupdate\fR [\fIname\fR[@\fIref\fR] .\&.\&.\&]
.RS 4
Update to the newest version of the same major version, one library at a time,
with rollback; a newer major version is only announced.\& With \fIname\fR@\fIref\fR switch
that library to an explicit version instead: a registry version, or for git
libraries a tag, branch, \fBHEAD\fR or full commit hash (for example \fBc3l update
lib@HEAD\fR moves a tag-locked library to HEAD).\& Moving to another major version
fails if a library that requires it asks for the old one.\& A name that is not in
the lockfile is an error.\& With \fB--dry-run\fR only print what would change.\&
.P
.RE
\fBsync\fR
.RS 4
Make the project match \fIc3l.\&lock\fR: reinstall missing or modified libraries at the
locked version and verify against the locked checksum or commit.\& With
\fB--frozen\fR fail instead if \fIproject.\&json\fR and the lockfile list different
libraries, and never write the lockfile.\& A library that cannot be restored does
not stop the others: \fBsync\fR goes on, then exits with status 1 and names the
failures.\& \fB--fail-fast\fR stops at the first one.\& Each library is still restored
atomically.\&
.P
.RE
\fBsearch\fR \fItext\fR | \fBtag:\fR\fIname\fR
.RS 4
Search the registry (its \fI/search\fR API, else its \fIindex.\&json\fR) and c3c'\&s vendor
collection, by name and description.\& The vendor list is the one built into this
c3l, so a library added to the collection since is missing; \fBadd vendor\fR lists the
collection as it is now.\& \fBtag:\fR searches the registry only.\&
.P
.RE
\fBinfo\fR \fInamespace/name\fR
.RS 4
Show the registry record of a library: its versions and their checksums, and
whether the latest one suits this C3 release and platform.\&
.P
.RE
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print the version.\&
.P
.RE
\fBhelp\fR [\fIcommand\fR]
.RS 4
Print the usage text of \fBc3l\fR or of \fIcommand\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBcompletion\fR \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIfish\fR
.RS 4
Print a shell completion script.\& See \fBSHELL COMPLETION\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fBmigrate\fR
.RS 4
Convert a c3po \fIproject.\&lock.\&json\fR into \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& The same commits are locked
as git libraries; run \fBsync\fR afterwards to rebuild them as verified archives.\&
.P
.RE
\fBcheck\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Verify that the library in \fIdir\fR (default: .\&) can be published, without
uploading: \fImanifest.\&json\fR with \fIprovides\fR, a valid version, a clean working
tree, the library compiles, and the version is not yet on the registry.\&
Exit status 1 on any problem.\&
.P
.RE
\fBpack\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Write \fIname-version.\&c3l\fR (or \fB--output\fR): a zip with \fImanifest.\&json\fR at its
root and the repository files (git: tracked and untracked-not-ignored; not
\fI.\&git\fR, \fIlib/\fR, \fIobj/\fR or \fIbuild/\fR), \fIc3l.\&lock\fR included.\& The archive is
deterministic, the same tree gives the same bytes.\&
.P
.RE
\fBpublish\fR [\fIdir\fR]
.RS 4
Run \fBcheck\fR, \fBpack\fR and upload to the registry, then compare the registry'\&s
checksum with the uploaded file.\& With \fB--dry-run\fR stop before the upload.\&
.P
.RE
.SH PUBLISHING
.P
\fBpublish\fR needs a registry with an upload API.\& Registry types: \fIc3pkg\fR (www.\&c3pkg.\&eu;
detected by probing \fI/api/v1/packages\fR) and \fIstatic\fR (read-only, anything else).\&
.P
For c3pkg: create an API token under Settings, API tokens, and give it to c3l with
\fB--token-file\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fBC3L_TOKEN\fR or \fBC3PKG_TOKEN\fR.\& It is sent as
\fIAuthorization: Bearer\fR header and never appears on a command line.\&
.P
The package name is \fIprovides\fR in \fImanifest.\&json\fR of the library directory (see
\fBc3c init-lib\fR).\& The version is, in this order: \fB--version\fR, a semantic version tag on
HEAD (\fIv1.\&2.\&3\fR or \fI1.\&2.\&3\fR), \fIversion\fR in \fImanifest.\&json\fR, \fIversion\fR in
\fIproject.\&json\fR (\fImanifest.\&json\fR wins).\& If the manifest or the project file says
something else, c3l warns and the archive gets the chosen version; the files in the
repository are not changed.\& A version is \fIMAJOR.\&MINOR.\&PATCH\fR or
\fIMAJOR.\&MINOR.\&PATCH-prerelease\fR and can never be changed once published.\&
.P
The C3 version of the library is sent with each upload and checked on \fBadd\fR and
\fBinfo\fR: a different major.\&minor or a missing platform gives a warning (an error
with \fB--strict\fR).\&
.P
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.P
A library directory (a \fImanifest.\&json\fR and no \fIproject.\&json\fR) works too: \fBadd\fR installs
into \fI.\&/lib\fR (keep it out of git; it is never packed), lists only the dependencies you
asked for in the manifest'\&s \fIdependencies\fR, and writes \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\& Commit the lock: it is
how the library declares its dependencies, and it travels with the library, in its git
archive and in the package \fBpack\fR builds.\&
.P
c3c lists a library'\&s dependencies by name only and does not install them
transitively: every one must be in \fIproject.\&json\fR.\& \fBadd\fR and \fBupdate\fR therefore
follow the dependencies a library declares and add them all, flat, to \fIlib\fR and
\fIproject.\&json\fR, as one transaction.\&
.P
A library declares them in its \fIc3l.\&lock\fR: each direct entry is a requirement, from
the source it names (a registry the consumer has no library from yet needs
\fB--allow-host\fR), at least at the locked version for registry libraries, at the locked
tag, branch or commit for git libraries (\fBupdate\fR moves a tag like any other version).\&
Apps and libraries alike, \fIc3l.\&lock\fR is the only file c3l writes dependencies to.\&
.P
c3l also reads, but never writes, \fIvendor.\&c3l.\&requires\fR in a library'\&s \fImanifest.\&json\fR
(packages published by c3l 1.\&1), c3po'\&s \fIvendor.\&c3po.\&sources\fR (\fIc3po-version\fR 1) and
c3c'\&s plain \fIdependencies\fR names (no source: a warning, and \fBverify\fR fails until the
library is added).\& For each name the first wins, in this order: \fIvendor.\&c3l.\&requires\fR,
\fIc3l.\&lock\fR, \fIvendor.\&c3po.\&sources\fR, \fIdependencies\fR.\& Dependencies that \fIproject.\&json\fR lists for a
single target are part of the project too (\fBlist\fR, \fBverify\fR, \fBsync --frozen\fR).\&
.P
Versions are chosen as in Go (minimum version selection): the highest of all
requested minimums, never newer.\& Different major versions are an error.\& A cycle,
or a library requiring itself, is a warning (an error with \fB--strict\fR); each
library is installed once.\& Git sources other than github.\&com, codeberg.\&org and the
hosts of URLs given on the command line need \fB--allow-host\fR or an answer at the
prompt.\& More than 200 libraries are refused.\&
.P
.SH PRIVATE REPOSITORIES
.P
c3l runs \fBgit\fR for git libraries, so private repositories work with whatever gives
git access: an ssh key (\fIgit@github.\&com:me/lib\fR) or, for https URLs, a credential
helper (for GitHub: \fBgh auth setup-git\fR).\& git is never allowed to ask on the
terminal; when it fails, c3l shows what git said.\&
.P
The same repository as \fIhttps://host/path\fR, \fIssh://git@host/path\fR and
\fIgit@host:path\fR counts as one source.\& Libraries should name their dependencies with
https URLs, which work for everyone; to fetch them over ssh yourself, let git
rewrite them:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
git config --global url\&."git@github\&.com:"\&.insteadOf https://github\&.com/
.fi
.RE
.P
In CI, give git access to the other repositories: an ssh deploy key with the
rewrite above, or a token (in GitHub Actions a personal access token; the
built-in \fIGITHUB_TOKEN\fR reads only the repository being built):
.P
.nf
.RS 4
git config --global url\&."https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github\&.com/"\&.insteadOf https://github\&.com/
.fi
.RE
.P
.SH LOCKFILE
.P
Tab separated, one library per line, sorted by name:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
# c3l\&.lock v1
box2d	registry	https://www\&.c3pkg\&.eu	jecokef902/box2d	1\&.0\&.0	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.	sha256:4945\&.\&.\&.	direct	-
hex	git	https://github\&.com/konimarti/hex\&.c3l	-	v0\&.1\&.1	commit:3fa9\&.\&.\&.	commit:3fa9\&.\&.\&.	direct	-
.fi
.RE
.P
Columns: name, kind (\fIregistry\fR, \fIgit\fR, \fIvendor\fR or \fIpath\fR), origin, id, version, pin (checksum
or commit), what the installed file is checked against (the SHA-256 again for registry and
vendor libraries; for git \fIcontent:\fR and a SHA-256 over the names and contents of the
files in the archive, or the commit again in locks written by c3l 1.\&1), role
(\fIdirect\fR: added by you; \fIdep\fR: required by another library) and the comma
separated names the library requires (\fI-\fR for none).\&
.P
The origin is where the library is fetched from: the registry base URL (what
\fBc3c --fetch-url\fR gets, no trailing slash), the git repository URL, or the directory.\&
The id is \fInamespace/name\fR for a registry and \fI-\fR otherwise.\& Every line names its own
origin, so one project can mix registries.\& Library names stay unique: the same name
from two origins is an error (git URLs that differ only in a trailing \fI/\fR or \fI.\&git\fR, or
in case on github.\&com and codeberg.\&org, are the same origin).\& A file with another number
of columns is refused, and so is a line with an invalid name, checksum or commit: a
lockfile can come from someone else'\&s repository.\&
.P
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.P
\fBc3l completion\fR prints a script that completes commands and options.\&
.P
bash: add to \fI~/.\&bashrc\fR, or save the script in \fI/etc/bash_completion.\&d/c3l\fR:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
source <(c3l completion bash)
.fi
.RE
.P
zsh: add to \fI~/.\&zshrc\fR, after \fBcompinit\fR:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
source <(c3l completion zsh)
.fi
.RE
.P
fish:
.P
.nf
.RS 4
c3l completion fish > ~/\&.config/fish/completions/c3l\&.fish
.fi
.RE
.P
.SH EXIT STATUS
.P
0 on success, 1 when a command fails, 2 for a usage error (an unknown command or
option, a wrong number of arguments), 130 when interrupted (SIGINT or SIGTERM;
what the command changed so far is undone, a second signal stops at once).\&
.P
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.P
\fIC3L_REGISTRY\fR
.RS 4
Registry base URL for new installs.\& Overridden by \fB--registry\fR.\&
Default: https://www.\&c3pkg.\&eu
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_ALLOWED_HOSTS\fR
.RS 4
Comma or space separated git hosts that dependencies may fetch from, in addition to
github.\&com and codeberg.\&org.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_MAX_DEPS\fR
.RS 4
Largest number of transitive libraries one command may install.\& Default: 200.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_TOKEN\fR, \fIC3PKG_TOKEN\fR
.RS 4
API token for \fBpublish\fR, if no \fB--token-file\fR is given.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_REGISTRY_TYPE\fR
.RS 4
Same as \fB--registry-type\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3C\fR
.RS 4
The c3c executable.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_LOCK\fR
.RS 4
Lockfile name.\& Default: \fIc3l.\&lock\fR.\&
.P
.RE
\fIC3L_VENDOR_URL\fR, \fIC3L_VENDOR_API\fR
.RS 4
Where the vendor collection and its asset list are read from.\& Default: the
\fIlatest\fR release of \fIgithub.\&com/c3lang/vendor\fR.\&
.P
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.P
\fBc3c\fR(1)
.P
